* @title An out-of-range real literal is an erroneous real number
* @nonstandard Snoflake rejects a non-finite REAL; CSNOBOL4 yields inf
* @match error
* @expect ERRONEOUS REAL NUMBER
* A digit string can name a value beyond the real range. SPREAL fails the
* conversion, the literal draws the compiler's diagnostic, and the host
* never throws.
	X = .5
END
